 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-PLAY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SERVER
     MOVE 1 TO PL-ENTITY-ID
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO CT-SET-TYPE
     CALL "CONTENT-SET-COUNTS"
     MOVE 1 TO CT-OPEN
     MOVE "bow" TO WS-KEY
     PERFORM LOOKUP
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-BOW
     MOVE "crossbow" TO WS-KEY
     PERFORM LOOKUP
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-CROSSBOW
     MOVE "trident" TO WS-KEY
     PERFORM LOOKUP
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-TRIDENT
     MOVE "shield" TO WS-KEY
     PERFORM LOOKUP
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-SHIELD
     MOVE "arrow" TO WS-KEY
     PERFORM LOOKUP
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-ARROW
     MOVE "tipped_arrow" TO WS-KEY
     PERFORM LOOKUP
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-TIPPED
     MOVE "firework_rocket" TO WS-KEY
     PERFORM LOOKUP
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-ROCKET
     MOVE "apple" TO WS-KEY
     PERFORM LOOKUP
     MOVE WS-ID TO WS-APPLE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
*>   The use animation of an item by its key.
     MOVE "T28200 a bow is use class 2" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "USE-ITEM-CLASS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-BOW WS-CLASS
     MOVE WS-CLASS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T28200 a crossbow is use class 3" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 3 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "USE-ITEM-CLASS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CROSSBOW WS-CLASS
     MOVE WS-CLASS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T28200 a trident is use class 4" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 4 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "USE-ITEM-CLASS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TRIDENT WS-CLASS
     MOVE WS-CLASS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T28200 a shield is use class 8" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 8 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "USE-ITEM-CLASS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SHIELD WS-CLASS
     MOVE WS-CLASS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T28200 an apple is no use class" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "USE-ITEM-CLASS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-APPLE WS-CLASS
     MOVE WS-CLASS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T28200 no item and an unknown item are no use class" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE -1 TO WS-ID
     CALL "USE-ITEM-CLASS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-CLASS
     MOVE WS-CLASS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 5000 TO WS-ID
     CALL "USE-ITEM-CLASS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-CLASS
     ADD WS-CLASS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Projectiles: none in a survival inventory; an arrow in a slot, a tipped arrow in the off hand; a firework rocket only for a crossbow; a creative player needs none.
     MOVE 0 TO PL-MODE
     MOVE 2 TO WS-CLASS
     CALL "USE-ITEM-AMMO" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CLASS WS-AMMO
     MOVE "T28200 a survival player with nothing has no projectile" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AMMO TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO PL-MODE
     CALL "USE-ITEM-AMMO" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CLASS WS-AMMO
     MOVE "T28200 a creative player needs no projectile" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AMMO TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-MODE
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(12)
     MOVE WS-ROCKET TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(12)
     CALL "USE-ITEM-AMMO" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CLASS WS-AMMO
     MOVE "T28200 a firework rocket is no ammunition of a bow" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AMMO TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-CLASS
     CALL "USE-ITEM-AMMO" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CLASS WS-AMMO
     MOVE "T28200 a firework rocket is ammunition of a crossbow" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AMMO TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(12)
     MOVE 2 TO WS-CLASS
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(3)
     MOVE WS-ARROW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(3)
     CALL "USE-ITEM-AMMO" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CLASS WS-AMMO
     MOVE "T28200 an arrow in a slot is a projectile" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AMMO TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(3)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-OFFHAND-COUNT
     MOVE WS-TIPPED TO PL-OFFHAND-ITEM
     CALL "USE-ITEM-AMMO" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CLASS WS-AMMO
     MOVE "T28200 a tipped arrow in the off hand is a projectile" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-AMMO TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-OFFHAND-COUNT
*>   The charged projectiles of a stack (51): a count above 0 is a loaded crossbow.
     MOVE 1 TO PB-ISX-COUNT
     MOVE 0 TO PB-ISX-ADDED-COUNT
     CALL "STACK-CHARGED" USING PB-ITEMSTACK-X WS-CHARGED
     MOVE "T28200 a stack with no components is not charged" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-CHARGED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO PB-ISX-ADDED-COUNT
     MOVE 51 TO PB-ISX-TYPE(1)
     MOVE 1 TO PB-ISX-VALUE-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE X"01" TO PB-ISX-VALUE(1)(1:1)
     CALL "STACK-CHARGED" USING PB-ITEMSTACK-X WS-CHARGED
     MOVE "T28200 charged_projectiles with one projectile is charged" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-CHARGED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE X"00" TO PB-ISX-VALUE(1)(1:1)
     CALL "STACK-CHARGED" USING PB-ITEMSTACK-X WS-CHARGED
     MOVE "T28200 charged_projectiles that is empty is not charged" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-CHARGED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 13 TO PB-ISX-TYPE(1)
     MOVE X"02" TO PB-ISX-VALUE(1)(1:1)
     CALL "STACK-CHARGED" USING PB-ITEMSTACK-X WS-CHARGED
     MOVE "T28200 another component with a value above 0 is not charged" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-CHARGED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   The slot takes the decision of the stack last decoded and loses it with the stack.
     MOVE 1 TO PL-STACK-CHARGED
     MOVE 5 TO WS-ARG
     MOVE 1 TO WS-COUNT
     MOVE WS-CROSSBOW TO WS-ID
     MOVE 0 TO WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ID WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "T28200 a loaded crossbow set into slot 5 keeps the charge" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-SLOT-CHARGED(6) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ID WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "T28200 emptying slot 5 clears the charge" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-SLOT-CHARGED(6) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ID WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-STACK-PUT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ID WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "T28200 emptying slot 5 with MENU-STACK-PUT clears the charge" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-SLOT-CHARGED(6) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 37 TO WS-ARG
     MOVE 1 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ID WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "T28200 a loaded crossbow in the off hand keeps the charge" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-OFFHAND-CHARGED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-HAND
     CALL "USE-ITEM-LOADED" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-HAND WS-LOADED
     MOVE "T28200 USE-ITEM-LOADED sees the loaded crossbow of the off hand" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LOADED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE WS-BOW TO PL-OFFHAND-ITEM
     CALL "USE-ITEM-LOADED" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-HAND WS-LOADED
     MOVE "T28200 a charged flag on a bow in the off hand is not a loaded crossbow" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LOADED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ID WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "T28200 emptying the off hand clears the charge" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-OFFHAND-CHARGED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-STACK-CHARGED PL-OFFHAND-COUNT
*>   The right button: survival, slot 0 held. A bow with no arrow begins nothing.
     MOVE 0 TO PL-HELD
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(1)
     MOVE WS-BOW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 20 TO WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "T28200 a bow with no arrow: the right button sends nothing and begins no use" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-USE-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE "T28200 no use state without an arrow" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
*>   With an arrow the press sends Use Item (main hand) and the bow is in use; the release sends Player Action 6.
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(3)
     MOVE WS-ARROW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(3)
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "T28200 a bow with an arrow: the right button sends Use Item with the main hand" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "4300010000000000000000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "T28200 the bow is in use (kind 2, main hand)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 20 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = PL-USE-KIND * 10 + PL-USE-HAND
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 5 TO WS-TICKS
     CALL "TEST-TICKS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TICKS
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "T28200 releasing the bow sends Player Action 6 (release use item)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "290600000000000000000000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "T28200 the use is over after the release" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-USE-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   A creative player needs no arrow; changing the held slot ends the use (release sent).
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(3)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-MODE
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     MOVE "T28200 a creative player draws a bow with no arrow" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-USE-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE 1 TO PL-HELD
     MOVE 20 TO WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "T28200 changing the held slot ends the use and sends Player Action 6" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "290600000000000000000000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 0 TO PL-HELD PL-MODE
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
*>   A trident begins a use of kind 4; the player dying ends it.
     MOVE WS-TRIDENT TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     MOVE "T28200 a trident in the main hand begins a use of kind 4" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 4 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-USE-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-HEALTH
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "T28200 the player dying ends the use" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-USE-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 20 TO PL-HEALTH
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
*>   A crossbow with an arrow begins a charge of 1250 ms (25 ticks) ...
     MOVE WS-CROSSBOW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(3)
     MOVE WS-ARROW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(3)
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     MOVE "T28200 a crossbow with an arrow begins a charge of kind 3 lasting 1250 ms" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 31250 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = PL-USE-KIND * 10000 + PL-USE-DURATION
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
*>   ... a loaded crossbow is fired by the press with no use beginning (Use Item sent, nothing kept) ...
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-CHARGED(1)
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "T28200 a loaded crossbow is fired by the right button: Use Item is sent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "4300050000000000000000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "T28200 firing a loaded crossbow begins no use" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-USE-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-CHARGED(1)
*>   A shield in the off hand with an empty main hand is raised with the off hand (Use Item hand 1); a main hand that holds food keeps its own use.
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(1)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-OFFHAND-COUNT
     MOVE WS-SHIELD TO PL-OFFHAND-ITEM
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "T28200 a shield in the off hand: Use Item with the off hand (hand 1)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "4301060000000000000000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "T28200 the shield is in use with the off hand (kind 8, hand 1)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 81 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = PL-USE-KIND * 10 + PL-USE-HAND
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(1)
     MOVE WS-APPLE TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     MOVE "T28200 food in the main hand is not given to the off hand's shield" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-USE-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     MOVE 0 TO PL-OFFHAND-COUNT PL-EATING
*>   A spectator uses nothing.
     MOVE WS-BOW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE 3 TO PL-MODE
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     MOVE "T28200 a spectator begins no use" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-USE-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-EV-BUTTON-UP TO WS-KIND
     CALL "TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-MS
     MOVE 0 TO PL-MODE
*>   The hand's mesh. The held item is the bow (a flat item); the view pose is the identity (no bob state), the equip height E 0.
     MOVE 0 TO PL-USE-KIND PL-EATING
     MOVE 0 TO CL-SWING-AT CL-BOB-INIT
     MOVE WS-BOW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(1)
     MOVE 0 TO PL-HELD
     COMPUTE CL-HAND-ITEM = WS-BOW + 1
     MOVE CL-HAND-ITEM TO CL-ATK-LAST
     MOVE 100 TO CL-ATK-TICKER
     MOVE 1 TO CL-HAND-H CL-HAND-OH
     MOVE 0 TO CL-OHAND-ITEM
     MOVE 0 TO CL-OHAND-H CL-OHAND-OH
     MOVE 3000000 TO CL-NOW-MS
     MOVE CL-NOW-MS TO CL-HAND-TICK-MS
     CALL "HAND-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE
     PERFORM MESH-CENTRE
     MOVE WS-CX TO WS-BX
     MOVE WS-CY TO WS-BY
     MOVE WS-CZ TO WS-BZ
     MOVE "T28200 a bow at rest has a mesh" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF RL-HAND-COUNT > 12
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   In use: the bow drawn for 10 ticks (kind 2), the trident 10 ticks (kind 4), the crossbow charged 12.5 of 25 ticks (kind 3): the mesh equals HAND-BUILD's for that kind.
     MOVE 2 TO PL-USE-KIND
     MOVE 0 TO PL-USE-HAND
     MOVE 0 TO PL-USE-DURATION
     MOVE 0 TO PL-USE-SLOT
     COMPUTE PL-USE-START = CL-NOW-MS - 500
     MOVE 2 TO WS-KIND2
     MOVE 10 TO WS-EL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-D
     MOVE "T28200 a bow drawn for 10 ticks is posed as HAND-ARM kind 2" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-USE-POSE
     MOVE 4 TO PL-USE-KIND
     MOVE 4 TO WS-KIND2
     MOVE "T28200 a trident held for 10 ticks is posed as HAND-ARM kind 4" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-USE-POSE
     MOVE 3 TO PL-USE-KIND
     MOVE 1250 TO PL-USE-DURATION
     COMPUTE PL-USE-START = CL-NOW-MS - 625
     MOVE 3 TO WS-KIND2
     MOVE 12.5 TO WS-EL
     MOVE 25 TO WS-D
     MOVE "T28200 a crossbow charged for 12.5 of 25 ticks is posed as HAND-ARM kind 3" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-USE-POSE
*>   A loaded crossbow that is still being held down is not charging: the pose of a crossbow at rest.
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-CHARGED(1)
     MOVE WS-CROSSBOW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     COMPUTE CL-HAND-ITEM = WS-CROSSBOW + 1
     MOVE CL-HAND-ITEM TO CL-ATK-LAST
     MOVE 7 TO WS-KIND2
     MOVE 0 TO WS-EL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-D
     MOVE "T28200 a loaded crossbow (use over or not) is posed as HAND-ARM kind 7" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-USE-POSE
     MOVE 0 TO PL-USE-KIND
     PERFORM CHECK-USE-POSE
     MOVE "T28200 a loaded crossbow in the main hand differs from the hand at rest" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-CX - WS-BX) > 0.01
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   A swing of a loaded crossbow 100 ms old is the swing pose, not the pose at rest; one that has just begun (progress 0, under 0.001) is still the pose at rest.
     COMPUTE CL-SWING-AT = CL-NOW-MS - 100
     MOVE 0 TO WS-KIND2
     MOVE "T28200 a swinging loaded crossbow is not posed at rest" TO WS-NAME
     CALL "HAND-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE
     PERFORM CHECK-BUILT-SWING
     MOVE CL-NOW-MS TO CL-SWING-AT
     MOVE 7 TO WS-KIND2
     MOVE "T28200 a swing that has just begun (progress 0) keeps the loaded crossbow at rest" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SWING
     PERFORM CHECK-USE-POSE
     MOVE 0 TO CL-SWING-AT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-CHARGED(1)
*>   The auto spin attack: pose 4 with a trident in the main hand (kind 6) or, with the main hand empty, in the off hand.
     MOVE WS-TRIDENT TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     COMPUTE CL-HAND-ITEM = WS-TRIDENT + 1
     MOVE CL-HAND-ITEM TO CL-ATK-LAST
     MOVE 4 TO PL-POSE
     MOVE 6 TO WS-KIND2
     MOVE 0 TO WS-EL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-D
     MOVE "T28200 an auto spin attack with a trident in the hand is posed as HAND-ARM kind 6" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-USE-POSE
     MOVE WS-BOW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     COMPUTE CL-HAND-ITEM = WS-BOW + 1
     MOVE CL-HAND-ITEM TO CL-ATK-LAST
     MOVE 1 TO PL-OFFHAND-COUNT
     MOVE WS-TRIDENT TO PL-OFFHAND-ITEM
     COMPUTE CL-OHAND-ITEM = WS-TRIDENT + 1
     MOVE 1 TO CL-OHAND-H CL-OHAND-OH
     MOVE 0 TO PL-POSE
     CALL "HAND-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-N0 = RL-HAND-COUNT / 2
     MOVE 4 TO PL-POSE
     CALL "HAND-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE WS-N0 TO WS-I0
     PERFORM OFF-CENTRE
     MOVE WS-CX TO WS-RX
     MOVE WS-CY TO WS-RY
     MOVE WS-CZ TO WS-RZ
     MOVE -1 TO WS-SIDE
     MOVE 6 TO WS-KIND2
     CALL "HAND-M-IDENT" USING WS-M
     MOVE 0 TO WS-E WS-EL WS-D WS-SWING
     MOVE 1 TO WS-LIGHT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FOIL
     MOVE 0 TO RL-HAND-COUNT RL-HG-COUNT
     CALL "HAND-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-M WS-SIDE CL-OHAND-ITEM WS-E WS-KIND2 WS-EL WS-D WS-SWING WS-LIGHT WS-FOIL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-I0
     PERFORM OFF-CENTRE
     MOVE "T28200 an auto spin attack with a bow in the main hand and a trident in the off hand poses the off hand as kind 6" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-CX - WS-RX) < 0.003 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-CY - WS-RY) < 0.003 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-CZ - WS-RZ) < 0.003
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   With neither hand holding a trident the spin attack poses nothing: both hands' meshes equal those of pose 0.
     MOVE WS-BOW TO PL-OFFHAND-ITEM
     COMPUTE CL-OHAND-ITEM = WS-BOW + 1
     MOVE 4 TO PL-POSE
     CALL "HAND-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE WS-N0 = RL-HAND-COUNT / 2
     MOVE 0 TO WS-I0
     PERFORM OFF-CENTRE
     MOVE WS-CX TO WS-RX
     MOVE WS-CY TO WS-RY
     MOVE WS-CZ TO WS-RZ
     MOVE WS-N0 TO WS-I0
     PERFORM OFF-CENTRE
     MOVE WS-CX TO WS-EX
     MOVE WS-CY TO WS-EY
     MOVE WS-CZ TO WS-EZ
     MOVE 0 TO PL-POSE
     CALL "HAND-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-I0
     PERFORM OFF-CENTRE
     MOVE "T28200 an auto spin attack with no trident in either hand poses nothing" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-CX - WS-RX) < 0.003 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-CY - WS-RY) < 0.003 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-CZ - WS-RZ) < 0.003 AND RL-HAND-COUNT > 24
         MOVE WS-N0 TO WS-I0
         PERFORM OFF-CENTRE
         IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-CX - WS-EX) < 0.003 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-CY - WS-EY) < 0.003 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-CZ - WS-EZ) < 0.003
             MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         END-IF
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-POSE PL-OFFHAND-COUNT CL-OHAND-ITEM
     STOP RUN.

 LOOKUP.
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ID WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS.

*> The mean of 12 vertices of the hand mesh from vertex WS-I0 + 1 on (the off hand's front and back quad when WS-I0 is the main hand's count).
 OFF-CENTRE.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-CX WS-CY WS-CZ
     PERFORM VARYING WS-J FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-J > 12
         COMPUTE WS-I = WS-I0 + WS-J
         ADD RL-HAND-X(WS-I) TO WS-CX
         ADD RL-HAND-Y(WS-I) TO WS-CY
         ADD RL-HAND-Z(WS-I) TO WS-CZ
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-CX = WS-CX / 12
     COMPUTE WS-CY = WS-CY / 12
     COMPUTE WS-CZ = WS-CZ / 12.

*> The mean of the first 12 vertices of the hand mesh (the front and back quad of the main hand's flat item).
 MESH-CENTRE.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-CX WS-CY WS-CZ
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 12
         ADD RL-HAND-X(WS-I) TO WS-CX
         ADD RL-HAND-Y(WS-I) TO WS-CY
         ADD RL-HAND-Z(WS-I) TO WS-CZ
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-CX = WS-CX / 12
     COMPUTE WS-CY = WS-CY / 12
     COMPUTE WS-CZ = WS-CZ / 12.

*> HAND-MESH under the state set, against HAND-BUILD with the identity prefix, E 0 and the pose kind WS-KIND2, elapsed WS-EL, duration WS-D, no swing.
 CHECK-USE-POSE.
     CALL "HAND-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE
     PERFORM MESH-CENTRE
     MOVE WS-CX TO WS-RX
     MOVE WS-CY TO WS-RY
     MOVE WS-CZ TO WS-RZ
     CALL "HAND-M-IDENT" USING WS-M
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SIDE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-E
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SWING
     MOVE 1 TO WS-LIGHT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FOIL
     MOVE 0 TO RL-HAND-COUNT RL-HG-COUNT
     PERFORM BUILD-NOW
     PERFORM MESH-CENTRE
     MOVE WS-NAME TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-CX - WS-RX) < 0.003 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-CY - WS-RY) < 0.003 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-CZ - WS-RZ) < 0.003
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

 BUILD-NOW.
     CALL "HAND-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-M WS-SIDE CL-HAND-ITEM WS-E WS-KIND2 WS-EL WS-D WS-SWING WS-LIGHT WS-FOIL.

*> The swinging loaded crossbow's mesh is not that of kind 7 at rest.
 CHECK-BUILT-SWING.
     PERFORM MESH-CENTRE
     MOVE WS-CX TO WS-RX
     MOVE WS-CY TO WS-RY
     MOVE WS-CZ TO WS-RZ
     MOVE 7 TO WS-KIND2
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SWING
     CALL "HAND-M-IDENT" USING WS-M
     MOVE 0 TO WS-E
     MOVE 1 TO WS-LIGHT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FOIL
     MOVE 0 TO RL-HAND-COUNT RL-HG-COUNT
     PERFORM BUILD-NOW
     PERFORM MESH-CENTRE
     MOVE WS-NAME TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-CX - WS-RX) > 0.003 OR FUNCTION ABS(WS-CY - WS-RY) > 0.003 OR FUNCTION ABS(WS-CZ - WS-RZ) > 0.003
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM TEST-USE-ITEM.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, event kind (CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN or CC-EV-BUTTON-UP), milliseconds: one CL-STEP that many milliseconds after the last with that right-button event.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CCSHIM.
 01 WS-EVENT.
    05 WS-KIND             BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-A                BINARY-LONG.
    05 FILLER              PIC X(16).
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-KIND                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-MS                   BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-KIND L-MS.
     INITIALIZE WS-EVENT
     MOVE L-KIND TO WS-KIND
     MOVE CC-BUTTON-RIGHT TO WS-A
     CALL "TEST-EVENTS-MS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EVENT WS-ONE L-MS
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TEST-RIGHT-BUTTON.
 COPY CLTEST.
